#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:2
msgid "Developing hotplug interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:4
msgid ""
"This page describes how developers can implement an {ref}`interface "
"<explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>` that supports [USB "
"hotplugging](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/v4.13/driver-api/usb/"
"hotplug.html),via snapd's built-in hotplug support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:6
msgid ""
"For a general user overview, including enabling this functionality and "
"hotplug interface management, see {ref}`Hotplug support <interfaces-hotplug-"
"support>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:8
msgid ""
"Hotplug support is currently {ref}`under active development <ref-"
"experimental-features_experimental-features>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:10
msgid "Adding hotplug interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:12
msgid ""
"The code for a snapd interface has be modified to support hotplug, and "
"subsequently create slots on the system snap, by implementing the following "
"new function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:14
msgid ""
"HotplugDeviceDetected(deviceInfo *hotplug.HotplugDeviceInfo) "
"(*hotplug.ProposedSlot, error)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:18
msgid ""
"When defined, `HotplugDeviceDetected` is executed whenever a *any* hotplug "
"device is connected to the system. The purpose of the function is to decide "
"whether a freshly connected device is relevant for any given interface by "
"returning one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:20
msgid ""
"if the connected device is not relevant, the function should return `nil, "
"nil`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:21
msgid ""
"if the connected device is relevant, a definition of the _proposed_ hotplug "
"slot that needs to be created should be returned (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:22
msgid ""
"if the connected device is relevant, but it’s impossible to create a slot "
"definition for it, an error should be returned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:24
msgid ""
"It is important to note that this function may be called multiple times as "
"the device connected because, in many cases, the kernel creates various "
"pseudo- and virtual- devices for given physical device. The function should "
"filter out irrelevant calls and only create a single slot definition for the "
"actual device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:26
msgid ""
"The returned slot is a _proposed slot_ because snapd’s hotplug subsystem "
"mediates the creation of the final slot. It may simply update the slot if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:28
msgid "the device is being reconnected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:29
msgid "the slot previously existed and had connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:31
msgid "Attribute access methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:33
msgid ""
"The above function receives the `hotplug.HotplugDeviceInfo` structure which "
"contains all the attributes provided by the udev event for the device, and "
"offers the following methods to access them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:35
msgid "**`Subsystem() string`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:37
msgid ""
"Returns the name of the kernel subsystem of the device, for example `tty` or "
"`sound`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:39
msgid "**`DeviceName() string`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:41
msgid ""
"Corresponds to udev’s `DEVNAME` attribute and provides the actual device "
"path, e.g. */dev/ttyUSB0*. This is the path that the interface is generally "
"interested in, as far as confinement rules are concerned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:43
msgid "**`DevicePath() string`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:45
msgid ""
"Corresponds to udev’s `DEVPATH` attribute and provides device path under the "
"sysfs filesystem, e.g. */sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:14.0/usb1/1-2*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:47
msgid "**`DeviceType() string`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:49
msgid "Corresponds to udev’s `DEVTYPE` attribute, e.g. *disk*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:51
msgid "**`Major() string`** and **`Minor() string`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:53
msgid ""
"Correspond to udev’s `MAJOR` and `MINOR` attributes which provide major/"
"minor device numbers (if applicable)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:55
msgid "**`Attribute(name string) (string, bool)`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:57
msgid ""
"A generic method to query any udev attribute. It returns false if the "
"attribute is not present in udev event data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:60
msgid ""
"The `hotplug.ProposedSlot` structure is created by `HotplugDeviceDetected` "
"in response to a udev event, and may define a name and label for the slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:62
msgid ""
"However, they are both optional and, in most cases, should be empty. Snapd’s "
"hotplug subsystem will automatically generate them by probing and sanitising "
"some of the well-defined udev attributes, such as model and vendor names. "
"This ensures the resulting name, whether provided by interface code or left "
"empty for snapd to figure out, is unique."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:64
msgid ""
"However, the `hotplug.ProposedSlot` must have some attributes set, and in "
"typical cases, should at least include an attribute that carries the path of "
"the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:66
msgid ""
"The path attribute can then be read by the following methods of the "
"interface (and others, as applicable), to create respective security "
"profiles for the snap and the given device:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:68
msgid "**`AppArmorConnectedSlot`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:69
msgid "**`SecCompConnectedPlug`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:70
msgid "**`SecCompConnectedSlot`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:72
msgid "Example implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:74
msgid ""
"The following is one potentially complete implementation of "
"`HotplugDeviceDetected`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:76
msgid ""
"func (iface *myInterface) HotplugDeviceDetected(di "
"*hotplug.HotplugDeviceInfo) (*hotplug.ProposedSlot, error) {\n"
"\tbus, _ := di.Attribute(\"ID_BUS”)\n"
"        // some arbitrary criteria to filter irrelevant devices out\n"
"\tif di.Subsystem() != \"tty\" || bus != \"usb” || di.Major() != „123” )  {\n"
"\t\treturn nil, nil\n"
"\t}\n"
"\n"
"\tslot := hotplug.ProposedSlot{\n"
"\t\tAttrs: map[string]interface{}{\n"
"\t\t\t\"path\": di.DeviceName(),\n"
"\t\t},\n"
"\t}\n"
"        return slot, nil\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:93
msgid ""
"When creating filtering logic for the above function, it is useful to "
"inspect udev attributes of the respective device. One way of doing this with "
"the is with the [udevadm](https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/"
"udevadm.html) command. This can be used to report all currently existing "
"devices (eg. `udevadm info -e`) or run in monitor mode (`udevadm monitor "
"-p`) to continuously report all udev event, along with their attributed, as "
"devices connected and unplugged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:95
