#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:134
msgid ""
"Snapd hardware interfaces, whose slots may appear as part of their {ref}"
"`gadget.yaml <reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>` "
"definition, for example, allowing `gadget` in their `allow-installation` "
"section of the base declaration, must additionally implement the following "
"function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:136
msgid ""
"HandledByGadget(deviceInfo *HotplugDeviceInfo, slot *snap.SlotInfo) bool\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:139
msgid ""
"The above function acts as a predicate that should return true if the device "
"described by `deviceInfo` is the same as the one represented by the given "
"slot. It’s called by the hotplug subsystem whenever a device is connected, "
"and it receives slot(s) of the given interface defined statically in "
"*gadget.yaml*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:141
msgid ""
"In the typical cases where gadget slots are defined by means of device "
"paths, the implementation of this method becomes a simple comparison of "
"device path and the path attribute of the slot, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:144
msgid ""
"func (iface *myInterface) HandledByGadget(di *hotplug.HotplugDeviceInfo, "
"slot *snap.SlotInfo) bool {\n"
"  var path string\n"
"  if err := slot.Attr(\"path\", &path); err != nil {\n"
"    return false\n"
"  }\n"
"  return di.DeviceName() == path\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:154
msgid "Hotplug and interface hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:156
msgid ""
"When a supported device is connected to the system, snapd creates a hotplug "
"slot for its respective interface. If the slot is then connected to a plug, "
"either manually by the user, or via the auto-connect mechanism, the "
"following interface hooks are executed if they exist:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:158
msgid "**`prepare-plug-<plugname>`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:159
msgid "**`connect-plug-<plugnname>`** (for the snap on the plug side)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:161
msgid ""
"Similarly, when the device is disconnected and its slot had been connected "
"to a plug, its `disconnect` interface hooks get executed, eg:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:163
msgid "**`disconnect-plug-<plugname>`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/developing-hotplug-interfaces.md:165
msgid ""
"This mechanism can be used by snaps to react to devices appearing/"
"disappearing from their connected plugs. Please refer to the documentation "
"on {ref}`Interface Hooks <explanation-interfaces-interface-hooks>` for more "
"details on this functionality."
msgstr ""
